---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/v2/BaseLayout.astro';
import NewsletterBlock from '../../../components/v2/NewsletterBlock.astro';
import { buildItemListSchema, buildBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../../lib/schema';
import { routeSlug } from '../../../lib/editorial';

const SITE = 'https://peninsulainsider.com.au';
const canonical = `${SITE}/wine/chardonnay/`;

const chardonnaySlugs = [
  'ten-minutes-by-tractor', 'kooyong', 'paringa-estate', 'polperro',
  'montalto', 'main-ridge-estate', 'yabby-lake', 'stonier-wines',
  'ocean-eight', 'scorpo-wines', 'red-hill-estate', 'pt-leo-estate',
];

const allVenues = await getCollection('venues');
const venues = chardonnaySlugs
  .map((s) => allVenues.find((v) => routeSlug(v) === s))
  .filter(Boolean) as typeof allVenues;

const itemListSchema = buildItemListSchema({
  name: 'Best Chardonnay producers — Mornington Peninsula',
  description: 'The Mornington Peninsula cellar doors producing the most compelling Chardonnay.',
  listPath: '/wine/chardonnay',
  items: venues.map((v) => ({ name: v.data.name, path: `/wine/${routeSlug(v)}`, itemType: 'Winery' })),
});

const breadcrumbSchema = buildBreadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: SITE },
  { name: 'Wine Country', url: `${SITE}/wine` },
  { name: 'Chardonnay', url: canonical },
]);

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + '/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Mornington Peninsula Chardonnay · Best Producers · Peninsula Insider"
  description="The Peninsula Insider guide to Mornington Peninsula Chardonnay — the producers making the most compelling cool-climate white in Victoria and what to look for."
  section="wine"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemListSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />

<section class="hero" aria-label="Chardonnay producers">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero__frame">
      <div class="hero__above">
        <div class="hero__meta">
          <span class="hero__meta-tag">Wine Country</span>
          <span class="hero__meta-divider"></span>
          <span class="hero__meta-date">Varietal guide <span class="ornament">·</span> Chardonnay</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="hero__headline">Mornington Peninsula <em>Chardonnay</em>.</h1>
        <p class="hero__dek">Where the region makes its most internationally competitive wines — cool-climate white at the elegant end of the Australian spectrum, closer to Burgundy in feel than to the richer, toasty styles.</p>
        <div class="hero__byline">
          <span>— By <strong>The Editors</strong></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <div class="hero__image ph ph-vine" role="img" aria-label="Chardonnay vineyard"></div>
        <figcaption class="hero__image-cap">
          <span>Chardonnay <span class="ornament">—</span> the Peninsula's white benchmark</span>
          <span>{venues.length} producers <span class="ornament">/</span> Red Hill to Merricks</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="letter" aria-labelledby="ch-letter">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="letter__frame">
      <div class="letter__body">
        <div class="letter__eyebrow">
          <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">Editor's Letter</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="letter__head" id="ch-letter">The Peninsula's white <em>benchmark</em>.</h2>
        <div class="letter__prose">
          <p>Chardonnay is the Peninsula's white benchmark and, arguably, where the region makes its most internationally competitive wines. The cool climate preserves natural acidity; the best examples sit at the elegant end of the Australian Chardonnay spectrum — closer to Burgundy in feel than to the richer, toasty styles that defined the variety in warmer parts of Australia.</p>
          <blockquote class="pullquote">The shift happened over the 2000s and 2010s — whole-bunch pressing, older oak, lower-intervention ferments. The results speak clearly.</blockquote>
          <p>Wines with texture, length, and the kind of citrus-and-stone character that reads well at a decade old. Ten Minutes by Tractor and Kooyong made the reputations early. The generation that followed — Polperro, Ocean Eight, Scorpo — has added its own vocabulary to the grape.</p>
          <p>The variety rewards patience: single-vineyard Chardonnay from a good producer in a good vintage is worth five years minimum.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="letter__sig">
          <span class="letter__sig-mark">—</span>
          <div>
            <div class="letter__sig-name">The Editors</div>
            <div class="letter__sig-role">Peninsula Insider · Wine</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="letter__side">
        <div class="letter__image ph ph-vine" role="img" aria-label="Chardonnay vines"></div>
        <figcaption class="letter__image-cap">Whole-bunch pressing and older oak — <em>the Peninsula method</em>.</figcaption>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shortlist" aria-labelledby="ch-list" id="producers">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="shortlist__frame">
      <div class="shortlist__intro">
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">Editorial ranking · {new Date().getFullYear()}</span>
        <h2 id="ch-list">{venues.length} Chardonnay <em>producers</em> worth seeking.</h2>
        <p class="shortlist__intro-body">Ordered by editorial authority and Halliday score.</p>
        <a href={`${base}wine/`} class="shortlist__intro-link">All producers
          <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14m-5-5 5 5-5 5"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
      <ol class="shortlist__list" style="list-style:none;">
        {venues.map((venue, i) => {
          const placeLabel = String(venue.data.place?.id ?? venue.data.place ?? '').replace(/-/g, ' ').replace(/\b\w/g, (l: string) => l.toUpperCase());
          const hats = venue.data.authority?.hats ?? 0;
          return (
            <li class="sl-item">
              <span class="sl-item__num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <div class="sl-item__body">
                <div class="sl-item__meta">
                  <span>{placeLabel}</span>
                  <span class="sl-item__meta-sep"></span>
                  <span>Chardonnay</span>
                  {venue.data.priceBand && <><span class="sl-item__meta-sep"></span><span>{venue.data.priceBand}</span></>}
                </div>
                <a href={`${base}wine/${routeSlug(venue)}/`} class="sl-item__name">{venue.data.name}</a>
                <p class="sl-item__why">{venue.data.signature}</p>
                <div class="sl-item__tags">
                  {hats > 0 && <span class="sl-item__tag sl-item__tag--hat">{hats} hat{hats > 1 ? 's' : ''}</span>}
                  {venue.data.authority?.hallidayScore && <span class="sl-item__tag">Halliday {venue.data.authority.hallidayScore}</span>}
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
          );
        })}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="letter" aria-labelledby="ch-faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="letter__frame">
      <div class="letter__body" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;">
        <div class="letter__eyebrow">
          <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">Frequently asked</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="letter__head" id="ch-faq">Questions on <em>Peninsula Chardonnay</em>.</h2>
        <div class="letter__prose">
          <h3>How does Mornington Peninsula Chardonnay differ from Yarra Valley Chardonnay?</h3>
          <p>Both regions produce fine, restrained Chardonnay, but the Peninsula has a more saline, mineral character driven by maritime influence. Yarra Valley Chardonnay tends to be slightly richer and more textural. The differences are real but subtle — both are among the best expressions of the variety in Australia.</p>
          <h3>Should you age Mornington Peninsula Chardonnay?</h3>
          <p>The single-vineyard and reserve labels reward 3–8 years. Estate labels are usually approachable within 1–2 years of release. The best Chardonnays — Ten Minutes by Tractor McCutcheon, Kooyong Faultline, Polperro Baillieu Vineyard — develop genuine complexity in bottle. Most cellar doors sell back vintages; ask at the counter.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<NewsletterBlock />
</BaseLayout>
